DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(x+3)^4");
$fun_1 = Formula("(((ln(x)))^2)^2");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("[5, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 19]) U [5, infinity)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("[5, infinity) U [5, infinity) U ((((-infinity, 19])))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-6, 2, 3} U {-6, 2, 3} U ([0, 9])");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(([0, 9] U [0, 9] U {-6, 2, 3} - ((-infinity, infinity) - [0, 9])) U [0, 9]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-6, 2, 3})) U [0, 9] U [0, 9] - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-6, 2, 3} - ((-infinity, infinity) - [0, 9])))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("[0, 9] U [0, 9] U (([0, 9]))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`11.42+0.71+19.77*6.34`]? [_____]{answer=>137.4718,width=>6}
---

[`8+10.57+19-7.53*15`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>-75.38,width=>3}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-6, 2, 3\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 0 \leq x \leq 9\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup A \cup (B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`((B \cup B \cup A \cap B) \cup B) \cap (A) \cup B \cup B \cap (A \cap B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cup B \cup ((B)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 19\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \geq 5\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 3 \leq x \leq 14\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup B \cup (((A))) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 4, 1, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 10, -3, 8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<4, 1, -3>") x Compute("<10, -3, 8>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<10, -3, 8>") . Compute("<4, 1, -3>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<4, 1, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<10, -3, 8>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, -3, 8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<4, 1, -3>") . Compute("<10, -3, 8>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, 1, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 5, -8, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 3, -7, -7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, -8, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, 1, -6>") . Compute("<5, -8, 1>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<5, -8, 1>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, 1, -6>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(8) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>8)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
